# APM Orchestration and Human Gates
<!-- cs: APM orchestrace a lidské brány -->

## Why band-based gates
<!-- cs: Proč brána podle pásma -->

A Human gate after **every** Task does not scale — it makes methodology overhead the
Human's main job instead of the project. The fix is not "skip review", it is "match gate
cost to actual risk", using the Task's band (`low`/`medium`/`high`, see `000-model-policy.mdc`
/ `AGENT_MODELS` config) as the deterministic trigger.
<!-- cs: Brána po každém tasku neškáluje — z metodiky se stane hlavní práce Humana místo
     projektu. Řešení není "přeskočit revizi", ale "přizpůsobit cenu brány riziku", podle
     pásma tasku jako deterministického spouštěče. -->

## A — Planner ↔ subagent protocol
<!-- cs: A — Protokol Planner ↔ subagent -->

Human runs the chat with the **Planner**; Planner spawns Coder and Reviewer as subagents.

- Give the Reviewer only `spec.md`, `dod.md`, and `git diff`. Mark `report.md` as a
  **claim to verify**, never as evidence — the Coder's own wording (e.g. "tests pass")
  must not leak into the Reviewer's prompt, or independence is lost even with a
  fresh-context subagent.
- **The parent window does not write code in Phase T** — except the `low`-band exception
  in §D below. Otherwise the `model:` audit trail breaks and code ships unreviewed.
- Read the verdict from `review.md`, never from your own summary of it.
- Resolve ambiguity **before** dispatching a subagent — it cannot ask follow-ups, so a
  vague Task Specification wastes an entire run.
- If a Coder subagent hits a question it cannot answer from `spec.md`, it returns the
  question to the **Planner**, not to the Human directly — the subagent did not open the
  chat with the Human and has no way to ask it.
- **Subagent completion signal** — a Coder/Reviewer subagent's final message to the
  Planner is exactly one of:
  - `DONE: <path to report.md or review.md>`
  - `BLOCKED: <one question>`

  No code, no diff, no prose summary in that message — the Planner reads the actual file,
  never the subagent's own account of it (same principle as "read the verdict from
  `review.md`" above).
- **Resuming after a chat window fills up** — start the new Planner chat with: *"Read
  `epic-NNN/plan.md` and the state of every task directory in it; continue from the first
  Task that has no `review.md` with verdict APPROVE."* This is the standard handoff
  sentence, not a one-off instruction to reconstruct each time.
<!-- cs: Reviewerovi jen spec/dod/diff; report.md je tvrzení k ověření. Rodičovské okno
     ve fázi T nepíše kód (kromě výjimky §D). Verdikt čti z review.md. Nejasnost řeš před
     zadáním subagentovi. Coder subagent se ptá Plannera, ne Humana. Subagent hlásí
     přesně DONE: <cesta> nebo BLOCKED: <otázka>, žádný kód ani prózu. Nový Planner chat
