## B — Gate and report tier by band
<!-- cs: B — Brána a úroveň reportu podle pásma -->

| Band | Human gate (FT.7) | Report tier | Written by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `high` | Every Task | Full (6 sections, see `070-project-management.mdc`) | Coder |
| `medium` | None per Task — surfaced in the Epic Report table (§C) | Short: *What was implemented*, *Inputs/outputs*, *Regression test results*, *DoD* | Coder |
| `low` | None — Reviewer gate (tests/lint) + APPROVE is sufficient | Micro: 5 lines — what, files touched, gate result | Coder, or Planner directly (§D) |

A Task is not done without a Reviewer verdict in every band — for `low`, that may be the
deterministic gate alone if `AGENT_MODELS` intentionally leaves Reviewer `low` unassigned
(see `000-model-policy.mdc`); otherwise an explicit `review.md` APPROVE is required.
<!-- cs: Task není hotový bez verdiktu Reviewera v žádném pásmu — u low to smí být jen
     deterministická brána, pokud AGENT_MODELS záměrně nechává Reviewer low nepřiřazeného;
     jinak je potřeba explicitní APPROVE v review.md. Tabulka: high = brána po každém
     tasku, medium/low = ne, jen v Epic Reportu. -->

### Escalation raises the gate too
<!-- cs: Eskalace zvedá i bránu -->

Band escalation (second `REQUEST CHANGES`, see `000-model-policy.mdc`) raises the
gate/report tier to match the **new** band, retroactively for that Task. A Task that
escalated from `low` to `medium` no longer qualifies for a micro report — write the tier
of the band it escalated to.
<!-- cs: Eskalace pásma (druhé REQUEST CHANGES) zvedá i bránu/report na úroveň nového pásma,
     zpětně pro daný task. -->

## C — Human Gate Briefing
<!-- cs: C — Briefing pro lidskou bránu -->

Whenever the Planner actually opens a Human gate (`high`-band FT.7, FE.2 Epic Plan
approval, FER.2 Roadmap review), lead with this briefing — do not hand over a raw report
and wait:
<!-- cs: Kdykoli Planner otevírá bránu pro Humana, začni tímto briefingem — nehazuj mu jen
     surový report a nečekej. -->

```markdown
## Gate: <Task/Epic/Roadmap name>

**Where we are:** 1–2 sentences — position in the Epic/project, what's done, what's next.
**What changed:** 3–5 bullets, not the full report.
**Decision needed:** a concrete question or A-vs-B choice — never "please approve".
**If you do nothing:** the default behavior / consequence of inaction.
```

## D — Low-band exceptions
<!-- cs: D — Výjimky pro pásmo low -->

- **Parent-window implementation.** For a `low`-band Task, the Planner may implement it
  directly in the parent window instead of spawning a Coder subagent. Trade-off: no
  separate `model:` audit entry for that change — note it in `plan.md`'s Task row instead
  of a standalone `report.md`.
- **Task cap.** An Epic plans **6–8 Tasks**. If decomposition needs more, split into two
  Epics — a wider Epic degrades planning quality more than it saves ceremony.
<!-- cs: Planner smí low task napsat sám v rodičovském okně (poznámka v plan.md místo
